WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.860
No battery anywhere.

2
00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:05.020
Just a metal rod lying
across two metal rails,

3
00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.820
in a magnetic field.

4
00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:10.860
Slide the rod along the rails, and a
current flows through the resistor joining

5
00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:11.550
them.

6
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.840
Or spin a coil between
the poles of a magnet.

7
00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:19.130
The voltage rises, falls,
and reverses every half turn.

8
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:22.220
So what decides how big that voltage is?

9
00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:26.460
In this mission, you'll see why a moving
rod's free electrons get pushed along

10
00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:28.930
it, piling charge at one end.

11
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.510
Then you'll look inside
a simple generator,

12
00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:35.000
and track its voltage through
one full turn of the coil.

13
00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:39.080
Your mission: find out what
decides how big the voltage is.
